# Uses that scripts/test_layout.mbtx accepts although its rules reject them.
# Each entry is `<file> <rule> # reason`, one line per use, so every new use
# needs its own decision. Rules: async-test, async-intrinsic, testing-import,
# wbtest-testing-import, clock.
mttp_core/src/rt/random.mbt clock # default_random is the host boundary for jitter and boundaries; callers take a random source with it as the default, so deterministic tests never read host entropy.
mttp_core/src/router/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # Driver schedules writes at the 64 KiB boundary while white-box access measures the private upgraded byte-pair buffer; a successful public WebSocket exchange cannot establish retained storage or the exact next-byte backpressure boundary.
mttp_core/src/router/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # SimCoordination supplies cancellable signals for that private byte-pair storage test on every target; public Router responses expose sessions rather than the byte-pair state whose reclamation is checked.
mttp_digest/src/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # driver runs the nonce-exhaustion regression on every target; white-box access seeds the private count at fffffffe instead of making about 4 billion public sends or exposing a test-only API.
mttp_digest/src/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # sim.Feed verifies caller ownership of the exhausted challenge's 401 body in that white-box regression; a black-box fixture cannot seed the private count near its limit.
mttp_core/src/endpoint/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # Driver runs the async contract tests of private BufferedStream, ResponseOwner, LimitedInput and EventBody; these adapter types are intentionally absent from the public API, so they cannot be tested directly from a black-box package.
mttp_core/src/endpoint/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The shared sim BodyStream checker receives each private adapter directly, and sim Feed supplies its source; black-box tests cannot name those adapter types, so this separate sim import is needed alongside Driver.
mttp_core/src/client/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The Driver executes NoLimiter's async boundary test while white-box access places its private sequence at Int64.MAX; issuing that many public admissions is infeasible, so black-box tests cannot verify refusal before sequence reuse.
mttp_core/src/client/ratelimit/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The Driver schedules cancellation and gate handoff while white-box tests count private holder/waiter references; successful later requests alone cannot prove these references were reclaimed.
mttp_core/src/client/ratelimit/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The sim clocks advance virtual time while white-box tests measure private map sizes and sweep thresholds; public state() cannot reveal retained orphan entries, so black-box success alone cannot prove these resource bounds.
mttp_ng/src/tls/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # sim.pair joins two TLS sessions in memory while white-box access probes the private session's input BIO; what a read took from beneath and OpenSSL has not consumed is not visible through TlsConn, so a black-box test cannot show the one-record bound without a test-only API.
